@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Variant — the same PaymentGateway classifier shown as a class diagram (attributes/operations) vs a composite structure (parts/ports/connectors).
'   usecase:      Contrast "what it has" (class: attributes + operations) with "what it's made of" (composite: parts + ports + connectors).
'   complexity:   simple
'   domain:       Payments
' ============================================================================
title Example Composite Structure Variant - Composite vs Class

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' The SAME classifier "PaymentGateway" appears twice:
'   LEFT  — as a CLASS diagram: attributes and operations (external contract).
'   RIGHT — as a COMPOSITE STRUCTURE: internal parts, ports, connectors
'           (internal architecture).
' A class diagram answers "what state does it hold and what can it do?"
' A composite-structure diagram answers "what is it built from, internally,
' and how do the pieces connect?"
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

' ===== CLASS DIAGRAM VIEW ================================================
together {
  class PaymentGateway <<class>> {
    - apiKey : String
    - timeout : Duration
    + charge(amount : Money) : Result
    + refund(txnId : String) : Result
    + getStatus(txnId : String) : Status
  }
}

' ===== COMPOSITE STRUCTURE VIEW ==========================================
together {
  rectangle "PaymentGateway" <<structuredClassifier>> as csGw {
    port "pReq : IChargeRequest" as csReq
    port "pRes : IChargeResult"  as csRes

    component "api : ApiFacade"      as csApi
    component "auth : Authorizer"    as csAuth
    component "bank : BankGateway"   as csBank
    component "audit : AuditLogger"  as csAudit

    csApi --> csAuth : authorize
    csAuth --> csBank : settle
    csBank --> csAudit : record

    csReq --> csApi
    csApi --> csRes
  }
}

note top of PaymentGateway
  <b>CLASS DIAGRAM</b>
  "What does it HAVE?"
  Attributes (state) + operations (behaviour).
  Hides internal composition.
end note

note top of csGw
  <b>COMPOSITE STRUCTURE</b>
  "What is it MADE OF?"
  Parts (roles) + ports + connectors.
  Reveals internal architecture.
end note

note bottom of PaymentGateway
  <b>"What it has" vs "what it's made of"</b>
  The class view lists the gateway's attributes and methods — its contract.
  The composite view decomposes the SAME classifier into collaborating parts
  and shows how requests flow from a boundary port through api -> auth ->
  bank -> audit.  Two diagrams, one type, two legitimate questions.
end note

@enduml
